WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.440
Oh, my, is that a souvenir for me?

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.200
Isn't he lovely?

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.780
I'll lend him to you once I'm done.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.950
Let's both enjoy ourselves together.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.250
What a predicament.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:26.750
We cannot accept any more guests.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.840
You really must restrain yourselves.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.760
I held back the whole voyage.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.180
Surely it doesn't matter if I snack a little.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.300
I know how you feel,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.060
but we are heresy in this country.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.600
Forebear until the deal progresses.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:49.980
The plan I am advancing
for your sake could be ruined.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.740
Besides which, Mr. Defrott seemed angry.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.870
When did you become that brat's errand boy?

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.280
Defrott can do nothing.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.540
That's why we're trying
to build a paradise here.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:09.590
If possible, I'd like to rule
by force as usual, but...

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.130
Why worry?

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:14.630
Let's just leave this to Rufus.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:18.510
I mean, he has a pretty face, if nothing else,

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.510
and he made Ascra for us.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:25.730
If you say so, I won't object.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:29.020
I want to have some fun with this boy.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.990
You were born from a liquor cask, Rufus.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.990
Don't get ideas.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:41.990
No matter how far you go,
you can never surpass us.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.620
I am well aware.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:48.420
Rufus, bring me some Ascra later.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.130
It's really quite something.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.920
As you wish.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.420
Wait. Don't hog him all to yourself.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.430
Persona Non Grata

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.720
Miserable rain.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.810
It is later summer;
the weather is unpredictable.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.230
Society is just like this weather.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.740
I hear Colonel Maeda is in poor condition.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:21.820
It's my fault for letting
him push himself so hard.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:27.500
I hate to tell you this now, but I thought
you'd rather know sooner than later.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.910
What is it?

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.670
Special Forces Unit 16
has been officially disbanded.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:37.010
Incinerate the vampire unit plan
and all related materials.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.010
Do I have until year's end?

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:42.010
You have August.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.010
I couldn't postpone it any longer.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.350
How should I pass on the unit's duties?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.230
You needn't.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:53.110
They've decided to introduce
the latest technology from Britain.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.940
They've imported something, then?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:04.780
They're far more capable than the vampire
units you've worked hard to cultivate.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.160
A large force of the highest rank--S class.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.290
It's decided. Even the
Minister of War approved it.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.000
You'll hear more later.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.380
That's all.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.760
He's wavering.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.110
Misaki?

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.070
Did I wake you?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.820
Where am I?

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.490
A hospital.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.830
A friend of mine is in here, too.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:53.330
Then why are you in this room?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.710
Isn't this crepe-myrtle pretty?

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:59.670
There was a lot in my garden,
so I thought it'd make a good gift.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.260
Answer me.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.390
Tell me the truth behind human combustion.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.310
Leave.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.100
Those are case files, right?

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.520
If you look at them, you'll be shot.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.440
What about these?

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.020
"Mr. Yoshinobu Maeda"

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.490
Where did you get those?

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.860
They were next to the documents.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.030
Give them back.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.700
I will if you tell me the truth.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.750
It's scary to think Shutaro
was in a place like this.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.090
You've mentioned that name before.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.840
My childhood friend, Shutaro Kurusu.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:50.930
I have letters from him
up until he left for Siberia.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:54.940
I wonder what he's up to now.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.980
Weren't you notified of his death?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.900
He promised me he wouldn't die.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.650
I'm sure he's alive.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.620
A promise, huh?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.690
"Mr. Yoshinobu Maeda"

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:11.540
What?

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:14.500
Won't you tell me the truth?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.120
Leave.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.080
No, huh?

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.250
But I won't give up.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.590
I'll be back.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.340
Bye. Take care.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:40.770
Dear Mr. Maeda, pardon this short note.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:46.530
Ever since Father received his new post,
he's been like a different person.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:50.280
Could he be involved in something bad?

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.790
Please, stop Father.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.250
Dear Yoshinobu,

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.420
I will always

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:02.000
miss you dearly.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.750
Dear Yoshinobu,
I will always miss you dearly

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.350
Misaki.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.780
It won't be much longer.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:28.820
We mustn't waste a single drop of spilled blood.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.450
Come in.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.700
Excuse me, sir.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.580
Colonel Maeda disappeared from the hospital.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.250
Maeda has?

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:53.100
Will you be playing Abel?

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.430
Or perhaps the sinful Cain?

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:01.270
What is a vampire doing in a playhouse?

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.900
I thought you'd come eventually.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:06.570
It took you longer than I thought.

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.820
I think it was right around here

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:11.820
that I shared my blood with Misaki.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.910
That day, Misaki was terribly
frightened of something.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.540
Perhaps it was her fate
to meet with an accident.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.840
Or perhaps...

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.340
"I want to apologize."

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.640
That's what she said.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:05.830
Tell me, Rufus, has Okimura's messenger come?

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.710
Not yet.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:12.970
Providing official registrations
for all of you will take some time.

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:15.010
We can't wait any longer.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:20.220
Everyone here wishes
to walk the night of a new city.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.480
Please wait a little longer.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.770
Rufus, would you clean my room?

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.900
Oh, you broke him already?

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.740
I hadn't even had a chance yet.

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:35.820
I'll find a new one for you.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.530
Once I can go out on the town.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:41.200
Hurry up, liquor-cask boy.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.160
As you wish.

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.980
It should be about time.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:21.660
"I hope this high-purity
Ascra suits your palate."

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.870
What a joke.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:27.330
We will now begin the extermination in Yokohama.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.210
Return alive.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.420
Yes, sir!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.180
All units, attack!

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.710
Hey, don't rock it! I'll fall!

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:08.000
Sorry!

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.670
It is a small boat.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.710
A bigger one would stand out.
Then they'd spot us.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.050
Dump that baggage!

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:19.090
We need it for fighting vampires.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.140
Why did we ever decide to go by sea?

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:27.940
Because they'd notice us by land,
and it would be hard for us to move.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:30.980
But vampires can't swim.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:33.860
Whose idea was this plan, anyway?

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:35.610
Colonel Maeda's.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.280
I knew it.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.950
That's our colonel.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:44.030
I bet the enemy vampires would
never expect us to come by sea.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:46.660
Any vampires we let escape

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:51.380
will be eliminated by heavily armed
special forces troops encircling the area.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:55.130
That's the plan for this operation.

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:59.680
Let's pull this off for
Colonel Maeda in the hospital!

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:00.880
Yeah.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.140
I never thought I'd see him
collapse from exhaustion.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:06.140
He's human after all.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.930
He'd barely been sleeping.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:12.230
Thanks to which, we uncovered that place.

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:16.440
It was built as a customs
warehouse for foreign trade

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:20.320
and also a temporary storehouse
for imported goods.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:25.160
A natural place to find the Scotch barrels
that had the blood serum in them.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:29.460
Advance intel is that
it's crawling with S-classes.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:32.500
How are we supposed to beat that?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.880
We're almost to land.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.390
Are you ready?

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.150
Anytime.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.320
Then let's get started.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.820
Oh, I'll tell Yamagami.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:10.750
Yamagami, if vampires escape
this way, we'll stop them.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:14.830
I'm going to make this work, Maeda.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.880
Let's go!

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.010
No one's here.

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:32.890
Where are they?

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.110
It's me.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:41.440
Suwa.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:42.690
Any luck?

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:44.200
No.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:46.700
That leaves the first floor.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:47.780
Yes.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:57.840
What is that, Takeuchi?

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.460
A skunk ball.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:04.300
It's full of compressed
rotten fish and <i>natto </i>stink.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:06.680
I'm glad I've got a mask.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:09.220
Kurusu, we're going in.

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.220
Right!

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:16.310
Vampires, there are two roads open to you.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.480
One!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:22.610
Obey us, Special Forces Unit 16,
and you will receive blood and registrations!

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:23.440
Two!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.860
Refuse to obey, and--

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.400
Don't waste your breath.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.360
Huh?

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:34.250
What's going on?

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.580
No idea.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.630
Maybe they had a falling out.

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:41.040
You two, come here quick!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.960
Unranked are coming at us from the front!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.640
On our way!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.480
What is this?

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.030
Their leftovers!

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:07.280
We'll get them all.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:08.280
Right!

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.490
Huh?

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.540
Oh, it overheated.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.370
I can't use this anymore.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.050
Aim more carefully, Yamagami!

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:27.220
You need to hit their hearts to kill them.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.800
I'm trying!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:31.800
But there's too many. My ammo won't last!

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.510
Oh, hey, wait!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.320
I'm impressed.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:46.780
But we can't stop this many with just us.

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.570
What now, Takeuchi?

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:52.530
Signal the special forces unit
encircling the area.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:59.830
Then, we'll have to thin their numbers
as much as we can until morning.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:05.000
But if someone gets bitten,
it might create a new vampire, right?

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.090
That's how it works.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.760
We've got no choice.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:12.550
We're the only ones who can fight them.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.850
To the city!

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.780
Run! Hurry!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:38.830
It's hopeless. There are too many.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.790
Shit!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.760
It's just not effective enough on unranked.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.010
I'll need to make improvements.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:56.720
What the...?

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.600
Something dangerous is coming.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.940
What is this presence?

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:11.740
What's wrong, everyone?

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.070
Don't tell me those are...

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.240
Vampire units.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.950
They're already complete?

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.750
What's going on?

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:07.210
Weren't we the vampire units?

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:09.040
When Code Zero got started,

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:12.460
all members of Code Zero
were called vampire units.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:16.640
But the real vampire unit plan
Ltg. Nakajima envisioned

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.680
was for an undying force.

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:25.640
In other words, the creation of an
immortal combat unit made up of vampires.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:32.990
Looks like the plan was progressing
without our knowledge.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:36.410
But if they're battle-ready,

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:41.450
why weren't they sent with us
on this operation in the first place?

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:45.210
Colonel Maeda must have
planned it to fool the enemy.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:50.040
He would use vampire units more efficiently.

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:55.550
He'd use them for suppression,
not cause panic in the city like this.

00:19:55.550 --> 00:20:01.260
Then Colonel Maeda doesn't know
about these vampire units either?

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.890
Probably not.

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:06.270
Suwa and I will follow them.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:11.730
Yamagami, Kurusu, meet up with
Colonel Maeda and find out the truth.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.190
All right.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:15.280
Let's hurry, Yamagami.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:17.150
Huh? Hey!

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.200
Wait!

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:31.460
So, this is the finished product.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:33.960
Not bad, General.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:21:00.360
There are more things
in Heaven and Earth, Horatio,

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.740
than are dreamt of in your philosophy.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.210
Nakajima!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:17.260
You orchestrated the disturbance
in Yokohama, didn't you?

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:21.180
I completed the vampire unit
plan according to schedule.

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:23.550
I'm not asking about that!

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:31.060
I'm asking why you had all the S-class
vampires we planned to bring in killed!

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:36.610
The vampire units are a match
for the supposed highest rank.

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:39.030
Doesn't this prove their worth?

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.780
Nakajima, you--

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.580
We shared an ideal.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:53.290
Where did it go wrong?

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:55.710
I won't waver,

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:57.630
Okimura.

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:46.940
The Last Blue Sky
